    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385-a8">

                <pb facs="0841" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg831"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 10 in No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Benjamin to Acting
                        Consul Cridland.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richmond,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> Under the circumstances mentioned in
                    your private letter of the 25th ultimo, just received, your continued residence
                    in Mobile will not be disturbed until your government has had time to make such
                    disposal of the whole subject as may seem best to it.</p>
                <p>I doubt not that instructions will arrive in a month or two.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. P. BENJAMIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
